#: ../../../diagnostic/CMD_CPS_NON_CONFORMING_LOCATION.rst:10
msgid ""
"Warn if :command:`find_package` finds a CPS package from a location that "
"does not conform to the CPS specification for `Package Searching`_.  This "
"may happen because CMake searches for packages in more locations than are "
"officially specified by CPS.  If the severity level is ``SEND_ERROR`` or "
"higher, CMake will not cache the package location and subsequent configure "
"attempts will also fail.  Otherwise, the diagnostic is only emitted when "
"CMake initially discovers the package."
msgstr ""
